{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Glossary.GlossaryQuantumFlatness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Glossary.GlossaryQuantumFlatness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Defs"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumFlatness.curvature_absorbed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumFlatness.curvature_absorbed","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-quantum-flatness.lean#L40-L40","doc":"**Curvature absorbed by the 2-group**: `F_∇ = dB + [B,B]`.\n\nWas `curvature_absorbed : Prop`, so the instance chose the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumFlatness.bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumFlatness.bracket","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-quantum-flatness.lean#L36-L36","doc":"The bracket `[·,·]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumFlatness.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumFlatness.d","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-quantum-flatness.lean#L34-L34","doc":"The exterior derivative on 2-forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumFlatness.B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumFlatness.B","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-quantum-flatness.lean#L32-L32","doc":"The 2-form datum `B ∈ Ω²(A) ⊗ Ad(A)`.\n\nWas `two_form_exists : Prop` — \"the datum exists\" as a proposition the\ninstance chose. **Existence of data is expressed by having the field**,\nnot by asserting it: a `QuantumFlatness` cannot be built without\nsupplying a `B`, which is exactly what the old field was trying to say\nand could not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumFlatness.F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumFlatness.F","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-quantum-flatness.lean#L24-L24","doc":"The curvature `F_∇`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumFlatness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumFlatness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-quantum-flatness.lean#L22-L22","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumFlatness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumFlatness","kind":"structure","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-quantum-flatness.lean#L15-L40","doc":"Quantum flatness: the curvature F_∇ of the connection is\nabsorbed by the inner-automorphism 2-group INN(G_q).\n\nMaps to Mathlib: related to `CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Transport`\nbut requires 2-categorical infrastructure not yet available. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:glossary-quantum-flatness","label":"rem:glossary-quantum-flatness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-quantum-flatness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}